---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Wanderburg Captain Tier List? An Honest Comparison (0.9.14 EA)';
const description =
  'Looking for a Wanderburg captain tier list? Here is the honest comparison: what each EN captain is verified to do, the best pick by situation, and why we do not print invented S/A/B ranks.';
const ogImage = 'https://wanderburgguide.site/images/modules/still-press-siege.jpg';
const heroSrc = '/images/modules/still-press-siege.jpg';

/** Verified card facts only — no invented grades. */
const comparison = [
  {
    name: 'Norbert The Normal',
    role: 'Default / baseline',
    pair: 'Any kit',
    verdict: 'Safe first pick. Keep him on while you learn slots — turrets+arrows tapes often stay here when no arrow captain fits.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Patchy The Pirate',
    role: 'Cannon damage',
    pair: 'Side Cannons, Front Cannon, mortar neighborhood',
    verdict: 'Strongest verified damage multiplier: all cannons +100% — enemy cannons too. The obvious "cannon build" captain.',
  },
  {
    name: 'The Count',
    role: 'Sustain',
    pair: 'Long Overtime sits, Repair Crew',
    verdict: 'Heals by consuming units (health boxes stop spawning on that kit read). Built for long, greedy Overtime farming.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Racer Ruth',
    role: 'Boost mobility',
    pair: 'Overtime kiting',
    verdict: 'Spoken kit: +50% speed when boosting, lower normal drive speed. The kite captain when you are not running Empress.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Tankbert',
    role: 'Hull / HP',
    pair: 'Front Ram / Arms, vehicle-kill routes',
    verdict: 'HP bar grows on destroying vehicles; nitro regen takes a -50% hit. Shop card still shows a 1,500 silver price tag.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Pyromaniac',
    role: 'Fire flavor',
    pair: 'Fire Crew + Side Ballista',
    verdict: 'Thematically the fire+ballista captain. Kit text is sparse on tape — confirm the tooltip before you spend silver.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Time Witch',
    role: 'Named on EN stills',
    pair: 'Read the tooltip',
    verdict: 'On the EN gallery, but kit text was not dumped on our tapes. Unranked until we can read it.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Duelist',
    role: 'Named on EN stills',
    pair: 'Read the tooltip',
    verdict: 'No verified melee/ram link on tape yet. Ram players: confirm in the loadout before buying.',
  },
];

const toc = [
  { href: '#why-no-tiers', label: 'Why no fake tiers' },
  { href: '#comparison', label: 'Honest comparison' },
  { href: '#by-situation', label: 'Best by situation' },
  { href: '#what-a-real-tier-list-needs', label: 'What a real tier list needs' },
  { href: '#empress', label: 'Empress note' },
  { href: '#faq', label: 'FAQ' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage} canonicalPath="/captains-tier-list/">
  <div class="editorial-hero">
    <img
      src={heroSrc}
      alt="Wanderburg siege fight — the best captain depends on how your run dies"
      width="1920"
      height="1080"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="editorial-layout">
    <article class="editorial-main">
      <h1>Captain Tier List? The Honest Comparison</h1>
      <p class="page-meta">Last Updated · Sep 13, 2026 · Early Access</p>
      <p class="editorial-intro">
        You searched for a Wanderburg captain tier list. Here is the honest version: what each captain is
        <strong>verified</strong> to do, which one fits your run, and why we will not invent S/A/B letters.
      </p>

      <section class="guide-section" id="why-no-tiers">
        <h2>Why we don’t print a fake tier list</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> A tier list needs <strong>full, verified kit text for every captain</strong> — and on
          0.9.9 EA tapes, two of the eight EN captains (Time Witch, Duelist) still have unread kit text, and two more
          (Lumberjack, Huntress) have no clean card art yet.
        </p>
        <p>
          Anyone printing exact S/A/B ranks right now is guessing — or inventing numbers. Several sites already rank
          captains that do not exist in the EN game (one ranks “Greta the Iron” and “Rolf the Steady” — no such cards on
          any EN shop tape). When a rank is a guess dressed as a fact, it costs you silver.
        </p>
        <p>
          What we can do honestly today: rank captains <strong>by situation</strong>, from card text that is readable on
          the shop stills. Full roster and pairing detail: <a href="/captains/">Captains</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="rankings-section" id="comparison" aria-labelledby="comparison-heading">
        <h2 id="comparison-heading">The honest comparison table</h2>
        <p class="meta-note">
          “Verdict” replaces a tier letter: what this captain is actually verified to do, and when that is worth silver.
        </p>
        <div class="rank-table-wrap">
          <table class="rank-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Captain</th>
                <th scope="col">Role</th>
                <th scope="col">Pair with</th>
                <th scope="col">Verdict</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {comparison.map((c) => (
                <tr>
                  <td class="rank-module">{c.name}</td>
                  <td>{c.role}</td>
                  <td>{c.pair}</td>
                  <td class="rank-when">{c.verdict}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="meta-note">
          Lumberjack (starter-flavored, rough card art) and Huntress (one tape reads ~50% auto-attack speed — try her on
          turrets+arrows) are in the between-run shop but stay out of the ranked table until we can read their cards
          cleanly. Source stills: <a href="/captains/">Captains</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="by-situation">
        <h2>Best captain by situation</h2>
        <div class="decision-tree">
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>First captain / learning the game</strong> → stay on <strong>Norbert The Normal</strong>. He is the
              default, fits any kit, and costs you nothing to keep.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Cannon build (side cannons / Front Cannon)</strong> → <strong>Patchy The Pirate</strong>. +100%
              cannon damage is the biggest verified multiplier in the roster — just remember enemy cannons get it too.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Farming Overtime silver</strong> → <strong>The Count</strong> (sustain for long sits) or
              <strong>Racer Ruth</strong> (boost kite). Empress also farms, but her half-speed tax is a real cost — see
              <a href="/silver-farming/">Silver farming</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Ram / vehicle-kill build</strong> → <strong>Tankbert</strong>. HP growth on vehicle kills fits the
              ram line; plan mobility elsewhere because nitro regen drops 50%.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Fire + ballista build</strong> → <strong>Pyromaniac</strong> looks like the fit (Fire Crew + Side
              Ballista) — confirm the tooltip before spending.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="what-a-real-tier-list-needs">
        <h2>What would make a real tier list</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Three things, none of which exist publicly yet: full tooltip text for all EN captains,
          a stable patch (EA balance moves weekly), and verified shop prices so “best per silver” can be computed.
        </p>
        <p>
          We hold this page to the same standard as the rest of the site: when kit text gets dumped on tape or the shop
          stills get cleaner, this table gets graded — and the change is dated. Unlock routes and silver cost context:
          <a href="/unlocks/">Unlock conditions</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="empress">
        <h2>What about Empress?</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Empress is spoken on EN tapes but is not in the EN gallery eight. Creators read:
          <strong>double friendly units</strong>, <strong>half speed</strong>. With Companion she doubles the hammer
          robot; the half-speed tax hurts Overtime — bring ram / booster / nitro. She is a build-enabler, not a flat
          “best captain”.
        </p>
        <p class="meta-note">
          Portuguese UI stills also show Kapitalistus Maximus and Sire Jonah — roster completeness only, not ranked
          against EN.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="faq">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <h3>Who is the best captain in Wanderburg?</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> For raw verified power, Patchy The Pirate (+100% cannon damage). For value, Norbert —
          he is free and fits everything. “Best” depends on your module family; the honest answer is a pairing decision,
          not a letter.
        </p>
        <h3>Is there an official Wanderburg tier list?</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Randwerk has not published captain rankings, and EA kit text is incomplete on
          tape. Any tier list you see right now — including ours if we printed one — would be an opinion, not data.
        </p>
        <h3>Should I buy Tankbert first?</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Only if you die to vehicle pressure and run a ram build — his HP growth scales with
          vehicle kills. Otherwise the first silver is better spent on the module unlock you just toasted (Front Cannon,
          Arms): <a href="/unlocks/">Unlock conditions</a> · <a href="/silver-farming/">Silver farming</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="crosslinks">
        <strong>Related:</strong>
        <a href="/captains/">Captains roster</a> ·
        <a href="/best-modules/">Best modules</a> ·
        <a href="/silver-farming/">Silver farming</a> ·
        <a href="/">Home</a>
      </div>

      <details class="still-checking">
        <summary>Still checking</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>Full tooltip text for Time Witch / Duelist / Pyromaniac — no clean dump yet.</li>
          <li>Clean card crops for Lumberjack / Huntress — pending, they stay unranked.</li>
          <li>Verified prices beyond Tankbert’s 1,500 silver shop card.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
    </article>

    <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="toc-label">On this page</p>
      <nav>
        {toc.map((item, i) => (
          <a href={item.href} class={i === 0 ? 'is-active' : undefined}>{item.label}</a>
        ))}
      </nav>
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
